[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3030248570","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/108068#issuecomment-3030248570","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108068","id":3030248570,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc60nex6","user":{"login":"TemporalCatcher","id":22987269,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyOTg3MjY5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/22987269?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TemporalCatcher","html_url":"https://github.com/TemporalCatcher","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TemporalCatcher/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TemporalCatcher/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TemporalCatcher/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TemporalCatcher/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TemporalCatcher/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TemporalCatcher/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TemporalCatcher/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TemporalCatcher/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TemporalCatcher/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-03T02:06:57Z","updated_at":"2025-07-03T02:59:48Z","body":"I decided to test it even more. It's even weirder. It may have something to do with exports.\n\nSo if I add the resources via `load` or `preload`:\n```gdscript\nvar tooless_resource := preload(\"res://toolless_resource.gd\").new()\n```\n everything works as intended. The usage is correct, and all functions act the correct ways too.\n\nHowever, when I add the `@export` annotation, and save the script twice (dunno why it must be twice), it goes from fine to what you get in the mrp. and when I remove the annotation and save script twice again, it goes back to being fine.\n\nand this weirdness was tested in both 4.0.stable and 4.5.beta2\n\n**Update:** Thanks to `@export_custom` I was able to find out the export problem has nothing to to with `PROPERTY_USAGE_EDITOR`, it has everything to do with `PROPERTY_USAGE_STORAGE`","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3030248570/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3704744654","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/108068#issuecomment-3704744654","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108068","id":3704744654,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7c0erO","user":{"login":"ColinSORourke","id":44822820,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0ODIyODIw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44822820?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke","html_url":"https://github.com/ColinSORourke","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-02T08:29:48Z","updated_at":"2026-01-02T08:29:48Z","body":"@TemporalCatcher I just tested this issue on build 4.5.1, and the prints seem to behave correctly.\n\n<img w